  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:5796",
  "verbalization": "Divaricataester C is implicated in the regulation of a sialyltransferase enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is targeted by multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate, both of which are linked to the activation of CX-1. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Divaricataester C may influence CX-1 through the modulation of this sialyltransferase. The evidence indicates that Divaricataester C could act as a modulator of the sialyltransferase pathway, potentially affecting CX-1 through a direct or indirect interaction. The consistent presence of CX-1 as a target across multiple pathways supports the hypothesis that Divaricataester C may exert its effects on CX-1 via the regulation of this enzyme. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple compounds that target the same enzyme and ultimately lead to the activation of CX-1, suggesting a plausible and biologically relevant pathway.",
